    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's just... the thought of it is what kills me. The idea of being a shell, sitting in a room, looking at people I love but not even knowing who they are. Or knowing them but not being able to tell them I love them because the words won't come. I'd rather just leave while I'm still me. While I still have my dignity. Does that even make sense? To want to go before the person you are is totally gone?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
